# Setup Guide — Smart Watering System

## Prerequisites

### Accounts Required
- [ThingSpeak](https://thingspeak.com) — free IoT cloud (MathWorks)
- [OpenWeatherMap](https://openweathermap.org/api) — free weather API (1000 calls/day)
- Gmail account with App Password enabled (for notifications)

## Step 1: ThingSpeak Channel Setup

1. Log into ThingSpeak → **Channels → New Channel**
2. Configure 8 fields:

| Field | Name | Units |
|---|---|---|
| Field 1 | Soil Moisture | % |
| Field 2 | Temperature | °C |
| Field 3 | Humidity | % |
| Field 4 | Light Level | lux |
| Field 5 | pH Value | — |
| Field 6 | Pump Status | 0/1 |
| Field 7 | ET0 Estimate | mm/day |
| Field 8 | Remote Pump Command | 0/1 |

3. Note your **Channel ID**, **Read API Key**, and **Write API Key**

## Step 2: Hardware Wiring

### ESP32 Connections
Component            ESP32 Pin    Notes
─────────────────────────────────────────
Capacitive Soil      GPIO 34      ADC1 only (3.3V safe)
DHT22 Data           GPIO 26      10kΩ pull-up to 3.3V
LDR / BH1750         GPIO 35      ADC or I2C (SDA/SCL)
pH Sensor Output     GPIO 33      ADC1, calibrate separately
Relay Module IN      GPIO 27      Active LOW
Relay VCC            5V           External 5V supply
Relay GND            GND          Common GND
LED (Status)         GPIO 2       Built-in LED
Water Pump           Relay NO/COM 5V pump, relay switched

- Use only ADC1 pins (32–39) for analog — ADC2 conflicts with WiFi
- Do NOT connect soil sensor directly to 5V ADC pins
- Use a flyback diode across pump motor terminals

## Step 3: Arduino IDE Setup

1. Install **Arduino IDE 2.x** from arduino.cc
2. Add ESP32 board package:
   - File → Preferences → Additional Boards Manager URLs:
   - `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/espressif/arduino-esp32/gh-pages/package_esp32_index.json`
3. Tools → Board Manager → Install **esp32 by Espressif**
4. Install Libraries (Tools → Manage Libraries):
   - `DHT sensor library` by Adafruit
   - `ThingSpeak` by MathWorks
   - `Adafruit Unified Sensor`

5. Open `src/arduino/main.ino`
6. Update credentials:
   ```cpp
   #define WIFI_SSID        "your_wifi_name"
   #define WIFI_PASSWORD    "your_wifi_password"
   #define CHANNEL_ID       1234567
   #define WRITE_API_KEY    "XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX"
   ```
7. Select: Tools → Board → **ESP32 Dev Module** → Upload
## Step 4: Python Environment

```bash
# Clone and set up
git clone https://github.com/your-username/smart-watering-iot.git
cd smart-watering-iot

# Create virtual environment
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate        # Linux/Mac
